## Proved condition

Positive nonzero raw x <= `00040000000000B1` and negative raw y in
[`BFF0000000000001`, `FFF0000000000000`] imply correctly rounded positive
infinity. The final endpoint y=-infinity is handled by its separate mathematical
limit; NaNs are excluded by the raw upper bound. The existing helper prefix
already limits y to finite magnitude below2^63, so its insertion point needs no
new nonfinite test.

`predicate-proof.json` verifies by exact rational arithmetic:

    alpha = 2^-52
    t = 177 * 2^-50
    ln(2) > 842/1215
    1024*alpha*(842/1215) - (1+alpha)*t > 0

Since ln(1+t)<t, the exact result exceeds2^1024. This is a sufficient condition;
no claim is made that every omitted case is finite.

## Placement established by real ARM execution

`parent-profile.json` contains seven actual completed R59 public calls, with
uncached instruction hooks and actual unchanged numerical bodies/ROM. Results
and costs exactly match the saved R59 DIRTY records. The subnormal gate is
reached after124–185 instructions, before the CR routine at135–196. Total parent
cost is6207–38473 versus788 for the fastest correct cached Qfplib composition.
Thus an implementation in the existing cold subnormal branch can be useful;
it does not suffer the earlier huge-y3000-instruction public prelude problem.

## Next implementation

Copy R59 source, original objects and linker inputs into this unfrozen successor;
compile only the modified `native_eabi_m0_rp2040.S`. Reuse exact R59 C++/other
objects. Put the new check at `.Lpow_subnormal_reciprocal_cut`, after the existing
positive nonzero subnormal x / finite negative y prefix. Normal x and all public
exact exponent shortcuts must retain their previous paths and counts.

The existing R4 is doubled magnitude-high(y), while R0:R1 and R2:R3 remain the
raw original arguments. R5/R6 are saved scratch registers. A possible guard is:

    compare R4 with 0x7fe00000
    if smaller: old_negative_cut
    if equal and R2==0: old_negative_cut
    compare R1 with 0x00040000
    if smaller: existing_positive_infinity_return
    if greater: old_negative_cut
    compare R0 with 177
    if <=177: existing_positive_infinity_return
    old_negative_cut: original instructions without modification

The high coefficient constant can use MOVS/LSLS;177 fits an immediate compare.
Use a single scalar literal for the exponent threshold if not already pooled.
This adds no lookup table. Preserve original arguments on every decline, SP/LR,
callee-saved registers and SIO. The original half-root/pow_rsqrt paths remain
unchanged, including subnormal inverse roots. M4/default objects remain exact.

First build and measure the seven cases against cached correct references.
